<title>FRANCE: Top 10 French regional airports for airfreight in 1996.</title>
<headline>Top 10 French regional airports for airfreight in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's top 10 regional airports for flown airfreight in 1996, with percentage change on 1995, were as follows, based on airport authority figures.</p>
<p> 1  Basle-Mulhouse *	 49,361 tonnes  up   27.0</p>
<p> 2  Marseille		  44,163 tonnes  up    3.0</p>
<p> 3  Toulouse		   25,503 tonnes  down  8.0</p>
<p> 4  Lille **		   24,376 tonnes  up    9.0</p>
<p> 5  Lyon-Satolas	     21,509 tonnes  up    9.8</p>
<p> 6  Nice			 18,103 tonnes  down  4.4</p>
<p> 7  Bordeaux		    8,270 tonnes  up    3.0</p>
<p> 8  Strasbourg		  6,492 tonnes  up    6.8</p>
<p> 9  Montpellier		 5,727 tonnes  up   19.5</p>
<p> 10 Ajaccio		     4,050 tonnes  up    9.4</p>
<p>*  includes traffic handled in Swiss zone of airport.</p>
<p>** also includes trucked air freight.</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
